aquinas-known-necessary.logic.r2: argue/scope: P3 (S2): read with the necessity on its consequent alone, our_known_necessary ∧ god_more_certain → (known_by_god → □be), the argument holds; read with it on the whole conditional, our_known_necessary ∧ god_more_certain → □(known_by_god → be), C1 (S2) does not follow: it needs the necessity of the consequent, not only of the consequence, and which the sentence means decides the argument
